          ]
        },
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $L$ be a finite integral framed link in the standard oriented $S^3$. In its complement choose an oriented knot $K$ with any integer framing and a small meridian $U$ of $K$, lying in a ball about one short arc of $K$ and disjoint from $L$. Give $U$ its disk framing zero. Then $L\\cup K\\cup U$ and $L$ are related by a finite sequence of orientation-preserving ambient isotopies, fully framed handle slides, and insertions or deletions of split $+1$ or $-1$ framed unknots. The conclusion applies also to the inverse insertion move. No condition on the knot type of $K$ or on its linking with $L$ is imposed.",
